# Paths in this directory that must NOT ship in the published chart package.
#
# `helm package` (the release workflow) applies this list when it builds the
# archive; `helm pull --untar` only extracts what was packaged. Every rule is
# anchored with a leading slash, so it matches only at the chart root and never
# a nested path such as templates/tests/ (Helm's test-hook convention).
#
# Who reads the excluded files, and why excluding them is safe:
# - A render from a Git checkout (the running demo Application, local work)
#   reads `--values` files and Argo CD's `.argocd-source-*.yaml` from the
#   repository, not from the package.
# - Argo CD does read `.argocd-source-<app>.yaml` from inside the chart when an
#   Application sources the published chart. The chart-sourced demo Application
#   (carverauto/gitops k8s/serviceradar-demo) takes values-demo.yaml from Git and
#   clears global.imageTag itself, so the chart version selects its images and it
#   needs neither file from the package.
#
# chart_package_contents_test.py pins this in both directions: these stay
# excluded, and the files operators are told to use from the package
# (values-ha.yaml, values-tenant.yaml, files/, templates/) stay included.

# Overlays and Argo CD overrides for ServiceRadar's own environments.
/values-demo.yaml
/values-demo-staging.yaml
/values-staging-demo.yaml
/.argocd-source-*.yaml

# Build and test sources, and what running the tests leaves behind.
/BUILD.bazel
/*.py
/tests/
/__pycache__/
